Build the image
docker build -t <name>:latest . 
name can be agent-test

Docker RUN to test locally first before tagging
Docker run -p 6034:6034 <name of image>:latest
ie Docker run -p 6034:6034 agent:latest

go on swagger localhost:6034/docs to verify whether it is working fine
now do control c and stop the process and kill the port




Log in to your Azure account  
az login --use-device-code 
this will give a code copy it and open the corresponding url from cmd itself, enter the code
we will be loging in CLI Azure
comeback to terminal and we will see our active subscribtions EA-AZ-DEV-AgenticAI_H&I is our subscription so press 1 and enter in cmd

Step 2: Log in to your Azure Container Registry  image is pushed in Container registry
Go to container registry and copy login server = ACR name

Replace `<acr-name>` with your ACR name(Our ACR Name – hexawarejarvisacr) 
```bash 
az acr login --name <acr-name>     
Using our ACR ---------     sudo docker login <acr name> 

Step 3: Tag your local Docker image with the ACR login server name 
```bash 
sudo docker tag <nameof image>: latest  <acr-name>/<nameofimage>:latest
name of the image is agent-test


Step 4: Push the image to your ACR 
 
```bash 
sudo docker push <acr-name> /<image name>:latest
``` 
Image name was agent-name
Now image gets mounted to ACR and pushed to ACR
